.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt INSTALL.SH 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm install.sh
.Nd symlink the Spacecentricity keymap into a QMK checkout
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar keymap_name
.Op Fl h | Fl -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is an optional POSIX-compliant script that creates a symbolic link from your QMK
keymaps directory to the root of this keymap repository, allowing QMK
to build this keymap without copying files into the QMK source tree.
.Pp
Optional man pages for this keymap’s helper scripts can be installed
separately with
.Xr install_man.sh 1 .
.Pp
By default:
.Bl -bullet
.It
The keymap name is
.Sq spacecentricity .
.It
The QMK checkout is assumed to be at
.Pa $HOME/qmk_firmware .
.El
.Pp
These defaults may be overridden:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Keymap name
Passed as a positional argument:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
install.sh my_keymap_name
.Ed
.It QMK root path
Set via the
.Ev QMK_PATH
environment variable:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
QMK_PATH=/path/to/qmk_firmware install.sh
.Ed
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Show the help message and exit.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev QMK_PATH
Path to your QMK firmware checkout.
Defaults to
.Pa $HOME/qmk_firmware .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal
install.sh
install.sh my_keymap_name
QMK_PATH=~/Projects/qmk_firmware install.sh
.Ed
.Pp
After installation, build the firmware with:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
qmk compile -kb inland/mk47 -km <keymap_name>
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr build.sh 1 ,
.Xr uninstall.sh 1 ,
.Xr install_man.sh 1 ,
.Xr license_headers.sh 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An LittleWalter
.Sh SOURCE CODE
.Lk https://github.com/LittleWalter/spacecentricity-mk47

